# {{.Package}}

CLI application scaffolded with [pal](https://github.com/zhulik/pal), a Go
dependency-injection and lifecycle toolkit.

Module: `{{.Module}}`

## Requirements

- Go 1.22+
- [Task](https://taskfile.dev/) (optional, for the Taskfile)
- [golangci-lint](https://golangci-lint.run/) (optional, for linting)

## Run

```bash
go run ./cmd/{{.Package}}
```

Or with Task:

```bash
task run
```

## Develop

```bash
task test
task lint
```

Coverage HTML report:

```bash
task cover
```

## Layout

```
.
├── cmd/{{.Package}}/   # application entrypoint
├── Taskfile.yaml       # test, lint, run
├── .golangci.yaml      # linter config
└── .gitignore
```

The entrypoint wires a `pal.Runner` with slog injection and standard init /
health-check / shutdown timeouts. Extend it by providing more services to
`pal.New` and injecting them into your runner.
